Circular ID: CIR-02 | Version: 1.0 | Effective: 2025-12-05 | Access: internal

Circular CIR-02 (CIR-2025-016) issued by AEON Credit Service (M) Berhad provi=
des operational clarification and documentary standards for identifying and e=
numerating dependants pursuant to Credit Policy v2 clause 3.2, which mandates=
 a higher Net Disposable Income (NDI) floor of RM 2,000 for applicants suppor=
ting three (3) or more dependants effective 2026-01-01.

1.0 - Purpose and Background
This Circular (CIR-02 / CIR-2025-016) provides binding underwriting guideline=
s for retail credit operations at AEON Credit Service (M) Berhad. Following C=
ircular CIR-2025-014 issued on 2025-11-20, which introduced the revised Net D=
isposable Income (NDI) threshold under Credit Policy v2 clause 3.2, credit un=
derwriting officers must verify and record the exact number of legal and fina=
ncial dependants supported by the primary financing applicant prior to approv=
ing any retail financing facility.

2.0 - Definition of Spouse Dependant
A spouse qualifies as an eligible dependant if legally married to the applica=
nt under Malaysian law (or foreign equivalent registered with the National Re=
gistration Department) and currently earning no independent gross personal in=
come. Non-working spouses include full-time homemakers and unemployed partner=
s. If the spouse earns demonstrable independent income or holds salaried empl=
oyment, the spouse shall not be counted as a financial dependant for the purp=
oses of the NDI assessment.

3.0 - Definition of Child Dependant
A biological, legally adopted, or formal foster child qualifies as a dependan=
t if the child is either: (a) under eighteen (18) years of age; (b) between e=
ighteen (18) and twenty-five (25) years of age and currently enrolled in full=
-time formal secondary or tertiary education (including certificate, diploma,=
 or undergraduate degree studies); or (c) physically or mentally incapacitate=
d regardless of age, certified by a registered medical practitioner. Gainfull=
y employed children earning independent wages must not be included.

4.0 - Definition of Parent and Senior Dependant
An applicant's biological, step, or legally adoptive parent qualifies as a de=
pendant where the parent resides with the applicant or receives primary finan=
cial maintenance from the applicant, provided the parent does not receive act=
ive employment income, commercial enterprise profit, or regular retirement an=
nuity exceeding RM 1,000 per month. Both the applicant's own parents and pare=
nts-in-law may qualify subject to verified primary financial dependency.

5.0 - Verification and Documentary Standards
Underwriters must obtain and verify authentic documentary evidence before ent=
ering the verified dependant count into the credit origination engine. Accept=
ed proofs include: marriage certificates or family card for spouses; birth ce=
rtificates or formal adoption orders for minor children; active student regis=
tration cards or official university acceptance letters for full-time tertiar=
y students; and medical certificates or statutory declarations for incapacita=
ted dependants and supported elderly parents.

6.0 - Interaction with NDI Floor and Credit Limits
Where the verified dependant count is zero (0), one (1), or two (2), the mand=
atory NDI floor after the proposed facility is drawn in full is RM 1,500. Whe=
re the applicant supports three (3) or more verified dependants, Credit Polic=
y v2 clause 3.2 strictly mandates an elevated NDI floor of RM 2,000. In all c=
ases, projected Debt Service Ratio (DSR) caps (60% for gross monthly income b=
elow RM 3,000; 70% for RM 3,000 and above) and initial limit ceilings (up to =
2x income below RM 5,000; up to 3x income at or above RM 5,000) remain concur=
rently binding.

7.0 - Audit Trail and Misrepresentation Penalties
All customer declarations regarding dependant counts must be cross-checked du=
ring verbal confirmation calls and verified against available database record=
s. Falsification, intentional omission of dependants to bypass the RM 2,000 N=
DI floor, or wrongful inflation of dependants constitutes credit non-complian=
ce. Underwriters failing to secure mandatory documentary proof prior to facil=
ity sanction will be referred to Credit Risk Governance for procedural audit =
review.
